	"EngineVersion": "5.8.0",
	"FriendlyName": "CoverPoints - Cover Point Generation, Scoring and Exclusive Reservation",
	"Description": "The cover in your level already exists - it is just written down nowhere. CoverPoints finds it once, scores it in constant time, and hands every point to exactly one agent. Drop a Cover Volume over an area and a grid is laid across the floor; each sample fires eight horizontal sweeps, and geometry found inside the cover distance becomes a cover point carrying the surface normal of the thing that shields it. A second sweep at standing height decides high cover against low cover, and three more decide whether an agent can lean out left, right or over the top - so PeekLeft, PeekRight and PeekOver are measured against the actual level, not guessed from a box. Generation runs in slices with a millisecond ceiling per frame and a visible percentage, because a level that freezes for two seconds while it builds is not a shipping feature. Queries cost no traces at all: the points sit in a coarse spatial hash, so 'best cover for this agent against that threat inside this radius' gathers a handful of cells and scores them on the angle between cover normal and threat direction, the distance to the agent, the distance to the threat, high against low, and which way the agent could peek. That is the difference from a hand-rolled solution that shoots a line trace per candidate and gets slower every time an artist adds a crate. Reservation is exclusive and it is the point of the plugin: Claim and Release with an expiry, so eight agents sent at once end up at eight different points and two never share one, even when the agent that held a point died without releasing it. A throttled verifier spends a fixed budget of line traces per frame spot-checking that a point scored as safe really does block - when one lies, it is invalidated on the spot and the counter says so. Everything it claims is on a Canvas statistics box that survives a Shipping build: points generated and how many are high or low, build progress and milliseconds per frame, queries per second, microseconds per query, points claimed, spot-checks run and points invalidated by them. Console commands Cover.Build, Cover.Stats, Cover.Show, Cover.Threat and Cover.Clear. What this is not: it is not cover behaviour. There is no Behavior Tree, no animation, no agent that walks itself into cover - it is the service underneath one, and it leaves the walking and the leaning to your character code. No UMG in the product, no Niagara, no Chaos, no editor module. Built and verified on Win64; Mac and Linux are enabled in the plugin descriptor but were not built for this release.",
	"Category": "AI",
	"CreatedBy": "Simulated Flow",
